                            <p></p><h3>Definition of "6j1":</h3><p><img src="/images/tubes/6J1_tube.jpg" class="shaft thumb" width="80" />6J1 is the designation for two different Chinese vaccuum tubes. It is a miniature pentode tube.</p><p>The newer version, reportedly manufactured by Shuguang, is equivalent to the EF95, 6AK5, and 5654 tubes. </p><p><img src="/images/tubes/6j1_lauten.jpg" class="shaft thumb" width="80" />The original version, manufactured by Peking Electron in the early 1980s, was a scientific-instrument grade tube, roughly equivalent to the Mullard M8100, the 6Ak5W, or the 6754W. These 6J1s are currently found only in Lauten Audio products. </p><p>See also this <a href="http://recforums.prosoundweb.com/index.php/m/336300/0/" rel="nofollow">6J1 tube discussion</a> and the review notes on our <a href="/microphones/CAD/Trion-8000" rel="nofollow">Trion 8000</a> writeup.</p>
